# T0183 — Per-user provider keys and feature unlocking

**Task:** T0183 (id 198) — AI: per-user provider keys and feature unlocking
**State at plan:** `ready` · Priority: high · Project: TaskMesh (4)
**Parent:** T0193 AI: Providers and keys (group). Design decisions are in epic T0177.
**Depends on:** T0182 complete (instance keys, `ai_key_mode`, `AI_CREDENTIALS_KEY`). Gate is clear.
**Branch (after approval):** `T0183-user-keys`
**Version on finish-up:** MINOR (new `drizzle/*.sql` for `user_ai_credentials`).

## Size

One feature: store each user’s provider keys, resolve the key for a request from `ai_key_mode`, and expose `GET /api/v1/ai/capabilities` so the client can show or hide the assistant. The settings page that edits those keys stays in T0190. Budgets stay in T0188. No split.

## Decisions

| # | Topic | Decision |
|---|--------|----------|
| 1 | Where keys live | New table `user_ai_credentials`. One row per `(user_id, plugin_id)`. Columns: `secret_enc` (same AES-256-GCM as instance keys, `AI_CREDENTIALS_KEY`), `hint` (last 4), `default_model` (nullable text), `verified_at`, `last_error` (nullable, capped), `updated_at`. `user_id` **ON DELETE CASCADE**. Plaintext never stored. |
| 2 | Who may write | The signed-in user, only their own rows. No administrator route to set another user’s key. |
| 3 | Which plugins | A non-local plugin that is loaded and **enabled** by the Administrator. Unknown, local, or disabled plugins are rejected. Local plugins (Ollama) never take a user key. |
| 4 | Write-only API | `GET /api/v1/ai/credentials` lists the caller’s rows: plugin id, hint, default model, `verifiedAt`, `lastError`. Never the key. `PUT /api/v1/ai/credentials/:pluginId` body `{ apiKey, defaultModel? }` replaces the ciphertext, clears `verified_at`, then verifies in the same request. `DELETE` removes the row. Responses, errors, and request logs never contain the key. |
| 5 | Verify on save | Decrypt only in memory and call the plugin `verifyKey`. Success sets `verified_at` and clears `last_error` (200). Provider rejection **keeps the row** with `verified_at` null and `last_error` set, and returns 422 with the redacted provider message. A stored key is usable at request time even when `verified_at` is null (same as instance keys). |
| 6 | Resolution | One function used by assistant session setup. Decrypt only for that call. **`instance_only`:** instance ciphertext, else the plugin env var. A user key is ignored. **`user_only`:** the caller’s key only. Instance ciphertext and env vars are never used. **`user_preferred_instance_fallback`:** the caller’s key when a row exists, otherwise instance ciphertext, otherwise the env var. Local plugins stay keyless in every mode. When the user’s row has `default_model`, that model is used for the call; otherwise the plugin’s configured chat model. |
| 7 | Capabilities | `GET /api/v1/ai/capabilities` (optional `projectId`). One entry for each registered feature. Today the only feature is `assistant`. Shape: `{ id, available, reason }`. `reason` is null when available, otherwise `no_key` \| `disabled_by_administrator` \| `project_excluded` \| `budget_reached`. |
| 8 | Reason rules | `disabled_by_administrator` when no enabled chat plugin can serve the feature. `no_key` when resolution yields no key for a non-local plugin (including `user_only` with no user row). `project_excluded` only when `projectId` is set and that project’s **effective** AI access is `excluded`. `read_only` does not hide the feature. `budget_reached` is in the enum and is never returned until T0188 wires the check. |
| 9 | Client | Top-bar **AI** button, Ctrl/⌘J, and `taskmesh:open-assistant`. When `assistant` is unavailable, the button stays visible, is disabled, and its title is a short sentence for that reason. The shortcut does not open the panel. Command palette “Open assistant” follows the same rule. No new settings form (T0190). |
| 10 | Chat path | `POST /api/v1/assistant/chat` and status use the same resolution for the signed-in user. An unconfigured result stays 503. The unconfigured copy mentions a personal key when the mode is `user_only` or `user_preferred_instance_fallback`. |
| 11 | Tests | Resolution: each of the three modes (user key used, user key ignored, instance/env refused under `user_only`, fallback order). Capabilities: no key, disabled plugin, `projectId` excluded, and budget reason absent. PUT/GET/DELETE bodies and error strings do not contain the submitted key. Cascade: deleting the user removes the row. |
| 12 | Docs | `docs/database/platform.md` for `user_ai_credentials`. Glossary only if a new enum needs a line (`reason` values live on the API, not in a system property). `npm run docs:sync-schema` after the doc edit. |

